<newsitem itemid="44475" id="root" date="1996-09-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Delta profits hit by exceptionals in H1.</title>
<headline>Delta profits hit by exceptionals in H1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 29</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.8		    vs 14.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.5		    vs 4.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     11.5		   vs 35.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   494.5		  vs 518.8</p>
<p> Operating result	 23.1		   vs 39.5</p>
<p> Exceptional charge     11.1		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		   5.5 payable	  vs 4.4 payable</p>
<p> Tax			  7.6		    vs 12.7</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.9		    vs 22.4</p>
<p> Attributable	     2.7		    vs 21.6</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2</p>
<p> Div registration date  September 24</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 16</p>
<p>Note - Electric cables and light engineering company Delta Plc said the start to the second half of the year &quot;has shown an improvement over recent months.&quot;</p>
<p>It said Robert Easton was stepping down as chief executive after over 22 years at the end of November. He will be replaced by Jon Scott-Maxwell who was with GKN.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
